Error [E0140]: `db` still owes `consume`
  --> tests/ui/single_use_dropped.jet:10:12
    |
 10 | fn run() { db :: acquire("db") }
    |            ^^
 Why: This value's type is `#SingleUse`, so it carries a job that has to be done — dropping it without doing that job leaves the work undone (an unjoined task, an unreleased lock)
 Fix: Consume it exactly once: move it to a parameter with the move marker `^`, or `return` it — or write `#Unsafe("reason") { consume(db) }` to discard it deliberately
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0140
